{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>In all My house he is trusted.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he is like a member of the household, who enters without permission and speaks whatever he needs." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'in all My house' — this is Beth-El, concerning which it is said (Genesis 31:13) ״אנכי האל בית אל״; it is 'the Good' concerning which it is said (Exodus 33:19) ״אני אעביר כל טובי״; and it is that in which our first father sinned and was not found trustworthy. Therefore it is said of Moses, 'in all My house he is trusted' — that is, he and not his father." "<b>And the view of</b> some of the kabbalists: 'in all My house' — this is the ב of בראשית, and it is the place of prayer, as it is said (Isaiah 56:7) ״ושמחתים בבית תפלתי״, and the expression 'my prayer' in the language of the Tiqqunim; and likewise (ibid.) ״כי ביתי בית תפלה יקרא״. And to this our Rabbis of blessed memory alluded in the matter of Hillel the Elder: the Holy One, blessed be He, said: if you come to My house, I will come to your house."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "The phrase 'באור' is taken as a reference to the Sefer ha-Tiqqunim; alternatively it may mean 'in explanation,' but the syntax is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:53.363421362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}